# Tech Trek — Core Rules

## Stack (locked — do not substitute)
- Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (Postgres, Auth with Google provider, Realtime)
- Judge0 CE via RapidAPI for code execution (hosted, not self-run — never attempt to self-host a judge)
- Deploy target: Vercel

## Source of truth
Everything in /docs is authoritative, especially Backend_Schema.md (schema) and
UIUX_Design_Brief.md (visual/animation direction). If code and docs disagree,
the docs win — flag the conflict, don't silently pick one.

## Non-negotiables
- Hidden test cases and the Judge0/RapidAPI key: server-side only, never in
  client code or client-visible responses.
- No destructive database or git operations without explicit confirmation first.
- No new paid service or dependency outside what TRD.md specifies without
  flagging it first.
- RLS policies from Backend_Schema.md stay enabled — never disable RLS
  "to make it easier to test."

## Process
- Work through Implementation_Plan.md in phase order. Verify a phase before
  moving to the next.
- Commit once per completed, verified phase, with a message naming the phase.
- Small ambiguities not covered by the docs: make the most consistent
  reasonable call, note it in a comment, keep going. Large ambiguities (data
  model, auth flow, anything costly to reverse): stop and ask.
